  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Famili i Redi Reintegration: Supporting Families to Maintain Healthy Relationships after Labour Mobility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Labour mobility has led to significant positive impacts for Ni-Vanuatu households, with participants using their earnings to meet both family and community needs &#x2013; especially in times of economic hardship due to COVID-19. There is a strong need, however, to support families to address the social impacts of the long-term separation which labour mobility involves, supporting them to maintain healthy relationships and achieve their financial goals both before the labour mobility period and as they reintegrate back into their communities upon their return.  IOM is partnering with UN Women to develop and deliver family-focused reintegration workshops to returned Ni-Vanuatu labour migrants: IOM will design and implement a series of family-focused reintegration workshops in Shefa Province.  These workshops will take the form of a core 3-day workshop on the reintegration process, focusing on themes related to healthy relationships and Ending Violence Against Women and Girls (EVAWG), and an optional two-day add-on session on entrepreneurship for participants who express an interest in establishing a business using their overseas work savings.  IOM will conduct stakeholder consultations with key EVAWG stakeholders in Vanuatu, as well as focus group discussions and interviews with former labour migrants and their families.</narrative>
  </description>
